    "done_when": "Give the repaired analytic limiter one owner for its designed contact, as the limiter rebaseline run (r-20261006T033955956303, merged c5f4b9766) recorded under follow_ons. Done when: (1) scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures/measure.py exposes the designed contact of limiter_contour's wall as one small public function (the midpoint of the vertical tangent edge at the outboard midplane, returned as an (R, Z) pair in metres), documented with the construction it relies on; (2) tests/test_topology_limiter_contact.py's geometric helper is replaced by that function, and benchmarks/limiter_read_resolution_audit.py and benchmarks/wall_at_cell_pitch.py, which still read the tangency as the (n-1)//2 vertex and so now point at the inboard side, read it from that function too; grep tests/, benchmarks/ and scripts/ once more for any other index-based contact reader and fix or list it; (3) the second-order contact assertion in tests/test_topology_limiter_contact.py is made truthful: on the repaired wall the contact lies on a vertical edge where the flux is stationary, so its radial error is exact by construction and its height error is roundoff (2.6e-15 m at 241 nodes, 6.2e-13 m at 481); the test asserts both rungs at or below a stated roundoff bound and its docstring says the contact is exact by construction, instead of claiming a 241-to-481 convergence order the operating point cannot exercise; (4) tests/test_topology_limiter_contact.py, tests/test_analytic_oracle_limiter_wall.py and tests/test_first_moment_centroid_row.py pass in per-module fresh processes by delta against main at dispatch, and each benchmark's import and its contact lookup run once on a small configuration with the printed contact at R = 7.80139579 m; (5) negative control: the old index-based lookup, run once against the repaired wall from a scratch copy, returns the inboard point and fails the new assertion. Before committing any log or receipt, run the shared path tool on it (the filepath relativize subcommand of nova.database.filepath, which rewrites worktree paths to repository-relative ones), because a commit hook will reject worktree paths. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync; these modules run in seconds, so the login node is acceptable with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv and PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree (orientation_worktree in the manifest); record baseline_suite and after_suite with module-qualified failure ids; commit with a conventional subject and a body; the manifest commits line lists every commit.",
